# The annotations of ZYNAPS.B's BASIC program (168 bytes at PROG = $5D3B, then TR-DOS's autostart mark): the single
# source of src/loader/loader*.asm (kit/mkgame.py --image; the format is kit/mkgame.py's
# class Annotations, plus @const). The image is work/parts/loader-5d3b.bin and the 4 autostart bytes after it.
#
# The code is what the analysis build work/stage2/loader (recording c1, frames 2051-2183: the loader from TR-DOS's
# LOAD to the intro's CALL) ran, widened by mkgame's walk.

@equ $1303 ROM_MAIN_4 ; the 48 BASIC ROM's MAIN-4: the report and the return to the editor after a statement
@equ $15BE ROM_CHANS_P ; the ROM's initial channel data, channel P's two addresses (output $09F4, input $15C4)
@equ $1B76 ROM_STMT_RET ; the ROM's STMT-RET: the next BASIC statement
@equ $3D13 TRDOS_ENTRY ; the TR-DOS ROM's entry for machine code: C = 5 reads B sectors from track D sector E to HL
@equ $5B00 Depack ; the Hrust 1 depacker (sector 1 of this file, src/loader/depacker.asm)
@equ $5C3D ERR_SP ; the system variable: the address of the error return on the machine stack
@equ $5C4F CHANS ; the system variable: the channel area
@equ $5CC2 TRDOS_HOOK 2 ; TR-DOS's RAM hook, called on its errors (a RET normally)
@equ $5CF4 TRDOS_NEXT 2 ; TR-DOS's track and sector after the last one read (E = the sector, D = the track)
@equ $6000 BlockStart ; where both packed blocks are read and unpacked in place: the intro's and the game's entry
@equ $C000 PagedSlot ; the top 16 K, the slot $7FFD pages

@module loader ; ZYNAPS.B's BASIC: the REM loader and its RUN line
@about TR-DOS's RUN "ZYNAPS" (the boot's list, or the user on the SCL) loads one sector of ZYNAPS.B: the catalogue says 168 bytes (one sector) of a file of 137. The program is two lines. Line 0 is a REM whose text is the loader's machine code from $5D40; line 1, the autostart line, is CLEAR VAL "24575": RANDOMIZE USR VAL "23872" (23872 = $5D40).
@about The loader reads the rest of the file by sector number from where TR-DOS's LOAD stopped (TRDOS_NEXT): sector 1, the depacker, to $5B00; 56 sectors (block 1, the intro) to $6000, unpacked in place and called; 79 sectors (block 2, the game) to $6000, unpacked in place. A key then starts the game's relocator at $6000.
@about The "2 in 1" is decided here: a paging test writes 1 (128K) or 0 (48K) over the high byte of line 0's number, $5D3B (Is128); the intro and the game's set-up read it. The intro later zeroes $5D40 and $5D41 (the first two bytes of this code, which ran once) and uses them as the option flags INF.LIVES and K-MOUSE.
$5D3B b Is128 ; line 0: the number (0; its high byte becomes the 128K flag), the length (139), REM
> The line number's high byte, $5D3B, is overwritten by SetIs128 with the paging test's result: 1 = the machine pages (128K), 0 = 48K. The intro (block 1) and the game's set-up (block 2) read it there. BASIC never runs this line again (the RANDOMIZE USR does not come back).
$5D40 c Loader ; the REM's machine code: TR-DOS's hook, the stack for BASIC, channel P, the 128K test, the loads
> Entered from line 1's RANDOMIZE USR VAL "23872". Writes POP AF: RET ($F1 $C9) to TRDOS_HOOK so a TR-DOS error returns quietly, then calls the next instruction, LoaderBody. Its first two bytes become the option flags later (the intro zeroes them: $5D40 INF.LIVES, $5D41 K-MOUSE).
$5D40 ; F1 C9: POP AF, RET
$5D46 ; the next instruction, as a call
$5D49 c LoaderBody ; the stack for a return to BASIC, channel P, the 128K test, the depacker, both blocks, a key, the game
> Reached by Loader's CALL (its return address is dropped at once). SP goes to the error return (ERR_SP), whose entry is replaced by ROM_MAIN_4 under ROM_STMT_RET: the shape of a USR's return, though nothing returns that way (the game never comes back). FLAGS bit 4 off (48 BASIC); channel P's addresses back to the ROM's.
> The paging test (IsItA128): $7FFD = $10 (bank 0, the 48 BASIC ROM) and $10 to $C000; $7FFD = $11 (bank 1) and $11 to $C000; $7FFD = $10 again and CP ($C000). On a 128K the read finds $10 (two pages): L = 1. On a 48K the port does nothing and the second write hit the same byte: $11, L = 0. Bank 1 keeps the $11, the only byte of it the program writes.
> Then the depacker to $5B00, block 1 read and unpacked and its intro called, block 2 read and unpacked, the border blue for three frames, a key, and JP $6000: block 2's relocator.
$5D49 ; the stack rebuilt so a later RET would end the statement in BASIC
$5D4A ; the stack at the error return (ERR_SP)
$5D4E ; drop it
$5D4F ; MAIN-4, under STMT-RET: the return path of a USR
$5D57 ; FLAGS bit 4 off: 48 BASIC
$5D5B ; channel P's output and input addresses back to the ROM's (TR-DOS's printer hook undone)
$5D6A IsItA128 ; the paging test: $10 and $11 to page 0's and page 1's $C000, then page 0 read back
$5D7F ; a 128K: L = 1 (H:L = $C001)
$5D80 SetIs128 ; the flag over line 0's number
$5D84 ; sector 1 (the depacker) to $5B00
$5D8C ; block 1 (56 sectors): read to $6000, unpacked in place
$5D91 ; the intro: the three pictures, the options, the tune (128K)
$5D94 ; block 2 (79 sectors): read to $6000, unpacked in place
$5D99 WaitKey ; the border blue for three frames, black, then a key
$5DA5 WaitAnyKey ; until any key of any row is down (IN A,($FE) with A = 0)
$5DAE ; the game's relocator (block 2's $6000)
$5DB1 c LoadBlock ; B sectors to $6000, then the depacker unpacks them in place
> Input: B = the sector count. Reads them through ReadSectors (TR-DOS goes on from TRDOS_NEXT), then JP Depack with HL = DE = $6000 (the packed block and its destination are the same place: the depacker moves the block to the end first). The depacker's RET returns to LoadBlock's caller.
$5DBF c ReadSectors ; B sectors from the next one TR-DOS would read, to HL
> Input: B = the sector count, HL = the address. C = 5 (TR-DOS's read), DE = TRDOS_NEXT; JP TRDOS_ENTRY, whose RET returns to the caller. Leaves TRDOS_NEXT on the sector after the last.
$5DC9 b Line0End ; line 0's ENTER, then line 1: number 1, length 21, CLEAR VAL "24575": RANDOMIZE USR VAL "23872"
$5DCA ; line 1: the number (big-endian), the length
$5DCE ; CLEAR VAL "24575": RAMTOP under $6000
$5DD7 ; : RANDOMIZE USR VAL "23872": the loader at $5D40
$5DE2 ; ENTER
$5DE3 b Autostart ; TR-DOS's autostart mark after the program: $80 $AA and the line, 1
